hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16846","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Isra'il ibn Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq informed us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us from his grandmother from her father Suwayd ibn Hanzala, he said: We went out intending the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and with us was Wa'il ibn Hujr, and an enemy of his seized him, and the people were reluctant to swear oaths, and I swore that he was my brother, and he released him. And we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I mentioned that to him, and he said: You were the most dutiful of them to him and the most truthful of them; you spoke the truth; the Muslim is the brother of the Muslim."
"16847","Al-Walid ibn al-Qasim and Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, they said: Isra'il narrated to us from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-A'la from his grandmother from her father Suwayd ibn Hanzala, he said: We went out intending the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned it."
